@baseUrl = http://localhost:5247
@yogaClassId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@spinClassId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@aliceActiveId = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
@bobInactiveId = bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb

### 1. Get all classes (and their real-time available spots)
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Get all members (active and inactive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/members
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Create a valid booking for Alice in Yoga -> 201 Created
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "memberId": "{{aliceActiveId}}",
  "classId": "{{yogaClassId}}"
}

###

### 4. Try booking Alice into Yoga again -> 409 Conflict (Booking.AlreadyBooked)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "memberId": "{{aliceActiveId}}",
  "classId": "{{yogaClassId}}"
}

###

### 5. Try booking inactive member Bob -> 422 Unprocessable Entity (Booking.MemberInactive)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "memberId": "{{bobInactiveId}}",
  "classId": "{{spinClassId}}"
}

###

### 6. Try booking with empty GUIDs -> 400 Bad Request (Result.Combine accumulates both field errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "memberId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "classId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

###

### 7. Cancel the created booking -> 204 No Content
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.$.id}}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Accept: application/json
